block head
    title Enteritis - Plants Cause Disease

block content
    h1 Enteritis
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/23049-enteritis-inflammation-small-intestine") Cleveland Clinic]:
    blockquote Enteritis is inflammation of your small intestine. The most common causes are viral and bacterial infections. Enteritis can also include your stomach (gastroenteritis) or your large intestine (enterocolitis). Enteritis caused by infection is often gastroenteritis. Common examples are food poisoning and the stomach flu.
